[00:20.00]Our happy God is merciful,
[00:24.93]His mercy not just dutiful.
[00:32.06]He takes delight in kindly deeds
[00:38.66]And freely grants our daily needs.
[00:45.43]Repentant ones can be assured
[00:51.42]Their plea for mercy will be heard.
[00:57.27]Remembering that we are dust,
[01:04.38]He’s merciful and kind and just.
[01:36.64]When we have sinned and feel distressed,
[01:42.56]When God’s forgiveness we request,
[01:49.04]Our Lord, Christ Jesus, showed the way
[01:54.53]To ask for mercy when we pray:
[02:01.94]“Forgive our debts, we beg of you,
[02:08.18]As we forgive our debtors too.”
[02:14.60]We then can let resentment go,
[02:21.02]And peace of mind and heart we’ll know.
[02:46.66]When gifts of mercy we bestow,
[02:52.96]The giving spirit we should show.
[02:59.30]We give without desiring praise,
[03:05.84]Content with joy our gift conveys.
[03:12.30]Then God, who sees all things we do,
[03:18.06]Will be the One repaying you.
[03:24.72]Yes, happy are the merciful,
[03:31.48]In God’s eyes they are beautiful.
